	(text "Notes:\n\n1.	TPS26631PWP load switch (implemented to ensure power is given to RPI only after 5V rail is stable)\n	a.	MODE pin on the TPS26631 in shorted to ground. This means that after an overcurrent event, the PMIC will automatically auto-retry\n	b.	UVLO threshold is 1.2V (min 1.176V, max 1.224V)\n		-	Given the resistor divider network provided, the nominal threshold voltage is 4.6V (min ~4.5V, max ~4.7V)\n	c.	External NFET is not used, so B_GATE and DRV are left floating\n	d.	We use the factory default OVP threshold of 34.4V for over voltage protection\n	e.	IMON is unused\n	f.	The 22nF capacitor on the dVdt pin gives a rise time of around 2.3ms\n	g.	ILIM is set to 6A\n2.	Buzzer circuitry\n	a.	Powered directly by GPIO pin\n	b.	Draws around 6mA of current, below the 15mA limit of the Pi's GPIO pins"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.066 43.688 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5c245d08-50cc-4ebe-a414-abe6205d9718")
	)
